---
// The admin is a real Astro route rather than a file in public/, so that the
// clean URL /admin/ resolves in dev, in `astro preview`, and on any host —
// files in public/ are served as assets and get no directory-index handling.
//
// The config it reads still lives at public/admin/config.yml.
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>CANDY Lab — Edit the website</title>
    <style>
      /* Shown only until the CMS bundle takes over the page. If the script is
         blocked or fails to load, this is what remains — a plain explanation
         rather than a blank white screen with no clue what went wrong. */
      #boot {
        max-width: 34rem;
        margin: 18vh auto 0;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
        font:
          16px/1.6 system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          sans-serif;
        color: #33475c;
      }
      #boot h1 {
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        color: #0e1c2b;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="boot">
      <h1>Loading the editor…</h1>
      <p>
        If this message is still here after a few seconds, the editor could not load. It is
        usually a network or sign-in problem rather than anything you did — reload the page, and
        if it happens again send this address to whoever maintains the site.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!--
      Sveltia CMS: a drop-in, actively maintained replacement for Decap CMS with
      a much better editing and media experience. It reads the same config.yml,
      so switching to Decap later is a one-line change.

      Every save becomes a git commit, which means every edit is revertable and
      the content never leaves this repository.
    -->
    <!-- No `type="module"`: the bundle is a classic script, and marking it as a
         module makes Sveltia warn that its JavaScript API will misbehave. -->
    <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/@sveltia/cms/dist/sveltia-cms.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
